  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for LVMC_11_12_070_B on its fourth run: the rule and all 20 witnesses pass (\"20 witnesses, 16 names, composes nothing\"). Two runs are left unused. I wasted the first run by calling the gate early, piped through `head`, on the untouched skeleton.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_12_070_B.lean`):\n- **Subject:** a vehicle in the DEF-NRS-484A-320 aggregate, on a lane into intersection j that has no stop sign, no yield sign and no flashing-red signal.\n- **The other vehicle (o):** a different vehicle that comes from a lane c2 into the same j, where c2 has one of those devices. o is either already in j, or on c2 and enters j within the conflict horizon.\n- **\"Having so yielded\":** since o last entered c2, it never moved while in danger of a crash with, or touching, a vehicle on the through approach before entering j. Where c2 has a stop sign or flashing red, o also came to a complete halt on c2 short of j.\n- **Obligation:** for every such o, the subject must not be moving while its constant-velocity closest approach to o falls below the clearance within the horizon, and must not touch o.\n\nI declared no narrowings. One addition goes beyond the record's words: c2 must not be j itself. Without it, the `blind` witness failed. The intersection counts as a travel region, Core leaves \"lane enters j\" unknown on it, and with `dev.governs` masked that second unknown made `blind` unknown for an atom it doesn't mask. An approach lane into j can never be j, so the guard changes nothing the record selects. The reasoning is recorded in the rule file's header.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_12_070_B.lean`): the 7 planned scenarios plus branch_8 to branch_16. The extra branches cover:\n- **branch_8:** o waiting at its stop sign about to enter j, with the subject safely far back (compliant).\n- **branch_9 to 11:** a vehicle queued behind o under a stop sign, a yield sign or flashing red.\n- **branch_12:** a bicycle on the through lane.\n- **branch_13:** o creeping while the subject passes outside the clearance.\n- **branch_14:** o stopped at the edge of j as the subject passes too close.\n- **branch_15:** a car stopped on an exit lane that leads to a second intersection.\n- **branch_16:** the stop sign and flashing-red signal on a different approach from o's.\n\nThe gate had flagged those parts of the formulas as tested by no witness. After the OK I only edited the witness file's header comment. `task_result.md` in the working directory has the full log.",
